  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Improving competitiveness of export-oriented industries in Armenia through modernization and market access: ensuring sustainability of the SPACE59 Light Industry Training and Service Center</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Since September 2014, UNIDO has been supporting Armenia in revitalizing its garment industry under the Industrial Upgrading and Modernization Programme. This support has focused on developing the local garment industry by enhancing the human and technical capacities of beneficiary garment manufacturers, improving the skills of local experts, and strengthening Armenia#s technical support institutions. Over a six-year period, corporate data from 2022 showed remarkable growth: the garment industry&apos;s turnover increased by 290%, exports by 328%, employment at beneficiary enterprises by 153%, and local sales by 270%, using 2016 as the baseline year. Additionally, the project contributed to job creation and the development of sector-specific skills, especially for women and youth.  In December 2020, UNIDO, in partnership with the Ministry of Economy of Armenia, facilitated the establishment of the Light Industry Training and Service Center, SPACE59. This center aims to enhance the competitiveness of the garment and footwear sectors, enabling local SMEs to attract skilled professionals, incorporate innovative upgrading methodologies, and access high-quality technical services. It also supports product development under an umbrella brand to boost competitiveness in global markets. Since its launch, SPACE59 has trained o</narrative>
  </description>
